.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1152 PM PDT Fri Oct 9 2026
(Tonight through Sunday)

Much cooler air quickly flowed inland Friday with about equally
weighted northerly ACV-SFO and onshore SFO-SAC pressure gradients
supporting northwest winds. Current 24 hour temperature trends
remain sharply lower by up to double digits Fahrenheit across
higher elevations and inland. Surface temperatures across the
highly varied terrain in our forecast area show only a few places
left at highest elevation that are still relatively mild from the
mid 60s to lower 70s. Due to a pattern shift with upper level
troughing forecast to dominate our weather through the weekend,
the lower level temperature inversion is already steadily weakening
and lifting. The marine layer depth continues to increase, currently
between ~ 1700 and 2500 feet. Cooling applied to the marine layer
with upsloping winds will produce light patchy drizzle from San
Francisco southward to the Big Sur coastline, including the East
Bay hills tonight and Saturday morning.

Cold air advection continues through Saturday greatly weakening
the lower level temperature inversion that`s capping the marine
stratus. Expect plentiful vertical mixing with drier air and
daytime surface heating to mix out the stratus by early afternoon.

Highs and lows Saturday and Sunday will be below to much below
normal for the time of year. Highs in the 60s/70s, warmest inland.
Lows in the 40s/30s, coldest far inland valleys, except near 50
along the immediate coastline and bays.

&&

.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1152 PM PDT Fri Oct 9 2026
(Sunday night through next Friday)

500 mb troughing will prevail with mainly drier air flowing
southward across our forecast area early to mid next week. There
may be a little light measurable shower activity in the southernmost
forecast area later Sunday and Monday. However, recent NBM has
trended drier to less than 0.10" liquid precipitation. 500 mb
ridging will advance eastward over our forecast area mid to late
next week, bringing a return to warmer daytime temperatures.

