.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1034 AM PDT Sat Oct 10 2026

A cold front is currently sweeping through the region helping to
scour out the cloud deck across Bay Area terminals this morning.
The fropa will usher in stronger winds as well. Expect a well
mixed BL this afternoon with stronger onshore flow. For tonight,
a little bit of strato-cu may develop over the hills and Monterey
Bay region. Will keep most terminals VFR, but have MVFR CIGs for
MRY and SNS with a 40-50% conf.

Vicinity of SFO...Improving CIGs through 18Z. Gusty onshore this
afternoon with gusts 25-30 kts.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Pre-frontal stratus lingering through 19Z
then mixing out as the front moves closer and eventually through.
Post frontal clouds late tonight and early tomorrow 1500-2000
feet.

