.MARINE...
(Today through Thursday)
Issued at 1034 AM PDT Sat Oct 10 2026

A passing cold front will continue to produce dangerous
conditions over the coastal waters this weekend. Fresh breezes to
Gale force northwest winds will occur. Expect frequent gale force
gusts in exposed waters along with rough to very rough seas
building in response to the strong winds. On top of the hazardous
winds and rough wind waves, two sets of swell haver arrived, from
both the south and west. The significant wave height will reach 16
feet in the northern outer waters.

&&

.BEACHES...
Issued at 1055 AM PDT Sat Oct 10 2026

Heading to the beach this weekend? The sun will be out, but
beaches conditions will be less than ideal. A cold front will
bring gusty winds over the coastal waters and nearby beaches.
More importantly, the surf zone will remain very energetic. Long
period southerly swell from distant Tropical Storm Rachel will
build in height through the weekend, bringing an increased risk of
sneaker waves and strong rip currents. Long period westerly swell
from a gale force low in the Central North Pacific will arrive
Sunday, bringing breaking waves 13-16 feet. The large tidal swings
will also result in coastal erosion as water and waves are
brought farther up the beach than normal, especially during high
tide. Remain off jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside
infrastructure as waves can sweep across the shoreline without
warning, pulling people into the sea. Remain out of the water to
avoid hazardous surf and strong rip currents and never turn your
back on the ocean!

